**Credit risk** = a **borrower does not pay interest or instalments** when due or on demand. It also arises:
- on **guarantees and letters of credit** when the liability **crystallises**;
- in **treasury products** when a **counterparty stops paying**;
- in **trading** when **settlement fails**;
- in **cross-border exposure** when **transfer of currency is restricted**.

**Lending is more than half** of a bank's risk-taking and is spread over **many branches**, so the policy must be **communicated across the organisation**.

**Framework**: answer **four questions** (what risks; which and how much to accept; how to monitor and control; how to reduce) through **identification, measurement, monitoring and control, mitigation**.

| Body | Role |
| --- | --- |
| **Board** | **overall responsibility**; **policies, procedures, aggregate limits**, reporting and audit; sets the **level of credit risk** |
| **Risk Management Committee** | **guidelines, conformity, prudential limits, robust models, staffing** |
| **CPC / CRMC** | policy on **credit proposals, covenants, rating standards, delegation, large exposures, concentrations, collateral, portfolio, loan review, pricing, provisioning** |
| **Credit Risk Management Department** | **independent of credit administration**; **enforces limits**, builds **rating and MIS systems**, **loan review** |

**Under the Reserve Bank's 2025 Directions** a bank must:
- have a **comprehensive Board approved credit risk management policy** (related parties, **country risk, unhedged foreign currency exposure**, valuation of properties, current/CC/OD accounts);
- follow the **Guidance Note on Credit Risk Management**;
- do **independent credit appraisal**, **not relying on outside or the borrower's in-house consultants**;
- run **sensitivity tests and scenario analysis for infrastructure projects** (delays, **cost overruns**);
- check the **source and quality of promoters' equity** (**no parent debt infused as subsidiary equity**);
- obtain **credit information reports** from credit information companies.
